 

DEVELOPMENT — .env (already exists, verify it's correct)
─────────────────────────────────────────────────────
File location: codelab-frontend/.env

VITE_API_URL=http://localhost:8080/api/v1
VITE_BASE_URL=http://localhost:8080



PRODUCTION — .env.production (create this new file)
─────────────────────────────────────────────────────
File location: codelab-frontend/.env.production

# VITE_API_URL=https://your-backend-domain.com/api/v1
# VITE_BASE_URL=https://your-backend-domain.com

VITE_API_URL=https://codelab-backend-l36z.onrender.com/api/v1
VITE_BASE_URL=https://codelab-backend-l36z.onrender.com

# When you deploy to Railway/Render/VPS, replace with real URLs
# Example:
# VITE_API_URL=https://codelab-backend.railway.app/api/v1
# VITE_BASE_URL=https://codelab-backend.railway.app


HOW VITE USES THESE:
─────────────────────────────────────────────────────
npm run dev    → uses .env                (localhost)
npm run build  → uses .env.production     (real server)

So you NEVER need to manually change URLs — just
run the correct command and Vite picks the right file.


IMPORTANT — .env files must NOT be committed to GitHub
─────────────────────────────────────────────────────
Both .env and .env.production are in .gitignore
Reason: they may contain secrets in production
Share config with teammates via a secure channel